 "post": {
  "title": "5 Signs Your Brain Is Stuck on Replay #shorts",
  "description": "Which sign got you? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who checked all five. Arthur is on day three of the same worry. In 'Nature experience reduces rumination and subgenual prefrontal cortex activation' (PNAS, 2015), Gregory Bratman, J. Paul Hamilton, Kevin Hahn, Gretchen Daily and James Gross had people take a 90-minute walk either through a natural area or beside a busy four-lane road. Only the nature walk lowered self-reported rumination and activity in the subgenual prefrontal cortex, a brain area linked to it. You're not broken. Just indoors. #psychology #shorts #overthinking #rumination #nature",
